[gd_scene format=3]

; Game Boy Advance SP primitive — a plain clamshell carrying NO licensed geometry.
; A complete model in its own right, not a shell bolted onto game_boy_advance_sp.tscn:
; its own row in SystemModelRegistry ("game_boy_advance_sp_primitive"), so a build
; can ship this and drop game_boy_advance_sp.tscn entirely.
;
; Fold rig, same convention as the NDS/3DS stand-ins: LidPivot sits on the hinge
; axis at the base half's back-top edge, the lid box and the live screen quad ride
; it, and LidPivot.rotation.x reads 0 = folded flat backwards … 180 = shut. The
; rest pose is 45 (135 deg interior) and the hinge stops at 30, which is as far
; past straight as a real SP opens.
;
; 82 x 84.6 x 12 mm per half — the real shell's 24.3 mm closed depth, split.

